  ← purpose : Apocky directive 2026-05-18 — "begin planning out GPU rendering and maturing this language for
                                                 a game engine capable of rendering 1440p 144hz or better efficiently"
  ← companion : 75_MENTAL_MAP_2026-05-18.csl (substrate-snapshot) · 77_LANGUAGE_MATURATION_ROADMAP.csl (language-axis)
  ← honors : spec/55 NORMAL_ENGINE_PIVOT (Forward+ mainline) + spec/59 GROK_VELOCITY_RESPONSE (revenue-first)
              + spec/32 SIGNATURE_RENDERING (substrate-effect-pass · DEMOTED-TO-OPTIONAL)
  ← prior-art-cited : LoA v14 (Odin+wgpu prototype · M1 achieved 144FPS@1440p Arc-A770) · 1LoA (math-substrate research)

§I THESIS
  ⟦
    Plan to mature CSSLv3 from "Forward+ scaffold compiles to MIR" into a sovereign · proprietary GPU rendering
    stack capable of 1440p @ 144Hz sustained (6.944ms / frame) on Intel Arc A770 reference HW · with headroom to
    144Hz @ 4K on RTX-50-class and 240Hz @ 1440p on future-HW. The plan is five sequenced phases — P0 (first-frame
    on screen) · P1 (1440p144 production-ceiling) · P2 (AAA-feature parity) · P3 (substrate-effect-pass opt-in) ·
    P4 (RTX-50 headroom + work-graph reach) — each gated by mechanically-verifiable observable-assertions. No phase
    advances by claim ; every phase advances by perf-timer + golden-frame-diff + symbol-audit. Substrate-rendering
    (spec/32 6-novelty-paths · 12-stage pipeline) stays as P3 opt-in effect-pass · DEMOTED per the 2026-05-03 pivot ·
    structural compatibility preserved. The renderer is proprietary all the way down : owned-CPU x86-64 backend
    (stage-1) · owned GPU emitters all four IRs at stage-2 (SPIR-V · DXIL · MSL · WGSL) · hand-rolled FFI per
    platform · zero rented runtimes · zero LLVM dependency at the IR layer. LoA v14 lessons absorbed : procgen-IS-
    renderer thesis (D-008 · validated at 144FPS@1440p Arc-A770 in M1) lands as opt-in bytecode-VM effect-pass in
    P3 ; AABB-pre-cull + bindless + subgroup-AABB-cull + TAA Halton-jitter + VRS-T2 + raw WM_INPUT all land as
    P1 perf-multipliers. 1LoA math-substrate (PGA Cl(3,0,1) Motor as entity-pose · SDF substrate-math · MLS-MPM
    as compute primitive) lands as P2 language-level upgrades (per items 61-67 in spec/63 + spec/65 GPU-memory).
  ⟧

§I OBSERVABLE-ASSERTIONS [MANDATORY · all-mechanical · all-verifiable-on-Arc-A770-reference-HW]
  ⟦
    ──── P0 · FIRST-FRAME-ON-SCREEN (visible-window milestone) ────
    ASSERT.P0.01 · `cssl-built engine.exe` opens a visible 2560×1440 window within 500ms of process-start
                    (per stdlib/window::window_spawn ; verified by Windows window-enumeration + bounds-rect probe)
    ASSERT.P0.02 · the swapchain clears the backbuffer to a non-default color (e.g. RGB 0x4A·0x40·0x80) for ≥ 60 frames
                    consecutively (verified by pixel-readback at center (1280·720) RMSE ≤ 1/255 from-target across 60 frames)
    ASSERT.P0.03 · per-frame budget : average present-to-present interval ≤ 7.0ms across 600-frame window @ 144Hz config
                    (verified by stdlib/time::time_monotonic_ns timestamp series ; report stored as JSON in dist/perf/P0_ms.json)
    ASSERT.P0.04 · WinMain-class regression : objdump --disassemble engine.exe shows user-main symbol at PE entry-point
                    (sentinel_build_check.sh PASS · Gate-E per spec/70 item-01·03)
    ASSERT.P0.05 · cssl-rt sentinel writes 0xC0FFEE + 0xDEADBEEF to %CSSL_SENTINEL_PATH% before/after user-main
                    (per spec/70 A01.1 + A01.2 · already IMPLEMENTED commit b7fb3e3)
    ASSERT.P0.06 · BLOCKER-α cleared : csslc cranelift-CPU backend emits valid object files for ALL 12 current engine
                    files (engine/{main · frame_clock · ecs · scene · render_forward · asset}.cssl + stdlib equivalents)
                    (verified by `csslc build --emit=object engine/main.cssl ; objdump engine.main.o ; cranelift-verifier exits 0`)

    ──── P1 · 1440p144 PRODUCTION-CEILING (canonical-target achievement) ────
    ASSERT.P1.01 · forward+ 5-pass scene (depth-prepass + light-cull-16×16 + opaque-main + transparent + post-tonemap) renders
                    a "canonical-1440p-test-scene" (50 lights · 200 visible meshes · HDR10 + sRGB targets) at
                    p99 frame-time ≤ 6.94ms across 10000-frame stress-run on Arc A770
    ASSERT.P1.02 · light-cull dispatch : 16×16 tiles × 256 threads (per engine/render_forward.cssl § light_cull constants)
                    completes within 0.8ms p99 for 256-light scene (verified by D3D12 timestamp-query per-pass)
    ASSERT.P1.03 · depth-prepass : per-mesh draw via Hi-Z occlusion-cull achieves ≥ 40% triangle-rejection on canonical
                    indoor-scene (verified by RenderDoc capture · pipeline-statistics query)
    ASSERT.P1.04 · TAA Halton-jitter (8-sample) eliminates per-pixel temporal flicker on canonical static scene
                    (verified by pixel-delta-RMSE between consecutive frames ≤ 2/255 over 100-frame window)
    ASSERT.P1.05 · VRS Tier-2 (per spec/56 ref) reduces fragment-shader cost by ≥ 30% on canonical foveated-scene
                    (verified by D3D12_FEATURE_DATA_D3D12_OPTIONS6 query + per-tile shading-rate readback +
                     ms-per-frame delta with VRS on vs off)
    ASSERT.P1.06 · bindless descriptor heap (per spec/14 § BACKEND-MATRIX VK_EXT_descriptor_indexing) supports
                    ≥ 4096 textures + ≥ 1024 buffers concurrently bound (verified by allocator stress-test)
    ASSERT.P1.07 · waitable-swap-chain mouse-to-photon : LOA_FRAME_LATENCY=1 (per stdlib/gpu) keeps mouse-input
                    → visible-cursor-move within 1 frame @ 144Hz (verified by high-speed-camera capture · ≤ 13.9ms)
    ASSERT.P1.08 · subgroup-AABB-cull warp-vote pattern (D3D12 wave32/wave64) prunes ≥ 30% sub-trees in stress-scene
                    (verified by D3D12 timestamp + sub-tree count counter on light-cull pass)
    ASSERT.P1.09 · all 5 passes pass-index ordinals stable per engine/render_forward.cssl § _test_pass_indices_are_distinct
    ASSERT.P1.10 · raw WM_INPUT path (per spec/56 D-028) keeps keyboard/mouse latency ≤ 1ms reflex-grade
                    (verified by GetTickCount delta · keypress-to-handler ≤ 1ms)

    ──── P2 · AAA-FEATURE-PARITY (advanced-rendering · pre-monetization-demo-quality) ────
    ASSERT.P2.01 · GPU-driven indirect-draw : visible-list culled + emitted on GPU · CPU writes zero per-mesh draws
                    (verified by D3D12 indirect-draw count + CPU-side draw-call counter == 0 in pass-2)
    ASSERT.P2.02 · async-compute Stage-3 + Stage-4 overlap : compute-queue runs Worley-noise procgen
                    in parallel with graphics-queue depth-prepass · GPU-utilization ≥ 92% on Arc A770
                    (verified by Intel GPU Performance Counters · GT_active_util ≥ 92% over 100-frame avg)
    ASSERT.P2.03 · cooperative-matrix (XMX via SPV_INTEL_subgroup_matrix_multiply_accumulate OR
                    KHR_cooperative_matrix) accelerates GBuffer-pack fp16 ops by ≥ 4× on Arc A770
                    (verified by per-pass timestamp delta · XMX-on vs XMX-off)
    ASSERT.P2.04 · shadow-map atlas with cascaded-shadow-maps (4-cascade · 2048² per cascade) renders sun-shadow
                    at < 1.0ms per frame on canonical outdoor-scene
    ASSERT.P2.05 · SSAO (HBAO or GTAO) on full-screen at < 0.4ms per frame at native-1440p
    ASSERT.P2.06 · screen-space reflections (SSR) on metallic surfaces < 0.6ms per frame
    ASSERT.P2.07 · bloom + tonemap (ACES-2 + per-channel transfer) total < 0.5ms per frame (per spec/32 Stage-10 budget)
    ASSERT.P2.08 · particle-GPU-sim : 100k particles · per-frame simulate+render < 1.2ms total
                    (verified by D3D12 timestamp + particle-counter readback)
    ASSERT.P2.09 · mesh shaders (D3D12 SM6.5+ / VK_EXT_mesh_shader) demonstrably render ≥ 1M triangles/frame
                    via meshlet pipeline at 1440p144 (verified by primitive-counter + p99 frame-time)
    ASSERT.P2.10 · spatial-audio HRTF mixing parallel with rendering (per spec/14 § HOST-AUDIO + cssl-host-audio)
                    < 256-frame buffer underrun-free for 1-hour soak-test
    ASSERT.P2.11 · drop-checker (per spec/63 item-30) catches GPU-resource leak in stress-test (100k Buffer alloc/drop
                    cycles · zero leaked handles per cssl-host-rt allocator audit)

    ──── P3 · SUBSTRATE-EFFECT-PASS OPT-IN (signature-rendering as opt-in mode) ────
    ASSERT.P3.01 · `engine.exe --substrate-effect=spectral-render` adds Stage-6 spectral KAN-BRDF on top of
                    forward+ opaque-main · per-pixel hero-wavelength + 4-accomp-N samples ; ≤ +1.2ms / frame budget
                    (per spec/32 Stage-6 Quest-3 ≤ 1.8ms · Arc-A770 expect ≤ 1.2ms with XMX cooperative-matrix)
    ASSERT.P3.02 · `engine.exe --substrate-effect=fractal-amp` adds Stage-7 sub-pixel-fractal-tessellation as
                    post-opaque-main displacement-pass · ≤ +0.8ms per frame (per spec/32 Stage-7 budget)
    ASSERT.P3.03 · `engine.exe --substrate-effect=gaze-collapse` adds Stage-2 fovea-mask + Σ-mask-update IFF
                    Cap<XR> granted + eye-tracker present ; ≤ +0.3ms · Sensitive<gaze> structural-refuse
                    (per spec/32 Stage-2 + spec/11 IFC + spec/22 telemetry)
    ASSERT.P3.04 · `engine.exe --substrate-effect=mise-en-abyme` adds Stage-9 recursive-witness · KAN-budget caps
                    recursion ≤ 4 · ≤ +0.4ms per frame (per spec/32 Stage-9 budget)
    ASSERT.P3.05 · `engine.exe --substrate-effect=wave-unity` adds Stage-4 LBM ψ-field multi-rate solver
                    on compute-queue concurrent with graphics-queue ; STRICT-ZERO LIGHT→MANA + AUDIO→MANA enforced
                    (per spec/32 V.1 R-4 + R-11 reimpl-contracts · grep-gate)
    ASSERT.P3.06 · `engine.exe --procgen-bytecode-vm` enables LoA-v14-style WGSL bytecode-VM evaluator
                    for procgen-IS-renderer mode · per-pixel rule-evaluation · 80-op stack-machine subset
                    (per LoA-v14 SUBSTRATE_BYTECODE_VM.md · ports to CSSL @gpu fn via cssl.gpu.* MIR ops)
    ASSERT.P3.07 · grep-no-RGB-mid : Stage-6 spectral source has no RGB conversion before Stage-10 tonemap
                    (mechanical-grep across cssl-spectral-render crate + emitted GPU IR shows zero RGB ops upstream of tonemap)
    ASSERT.P3.08 · grep-no-spy-mirror : Stage-9 mise-en-abyme uses true-recursive-ray-cast not cubemap-cache
                    (mechanical-grep + RenderDoc capture confirms cssl.rt.trace_ray ops · no cubemap-sample)

    ──── P4 · RTX-50 HEADROOM + WORK-GRAPH REACH (future-HW + emerging-tech) ────
    ASSERT.P4.01 · D3D12 Work Graphs 1.0 (SM6.8 · SV_DispatchGrid · record-based input/output nodes per Microsoft
                    devblog 2024-03) compiles via cssl-cgen-gpu-dxil with @workgraph_node attribute
                    (per spec/63 item-32 · UPG_02_HW_BACKEND § GPU-resident-state)
    ASSERT.P4.02 · VK_AMDX_shader_enqueue (Vulkan work-graph extension) emits via cssl-cgen-gpu-spirv equivalent path
                    (per UPG_02 + spec/63 item-32)
    ASSERT.P4.03 · @persistent_kernel attribute compiles to GPU-loop kernel that consumes work-items from queue
                    without CPU round-trip (per spec/63 item-31 · UPG_02 § persistent-kernels)
    ASSERT.P4.04 · RTX-50 reference test : canonical-1440p-test-scene runs at p99 ≤ 4.0ms / frame on RTX 5090
                    (= 240Hz headroom · verified by per-pass timestamp on test-bench)
    ASSERT.P4.05 · 4K@144Hz reference test : canonical-test-scene at 3840×2160 runs at p99 ≤ 6.94ms / frame on RTX 5090
    ASSERT.P4.06 · cross-target-struct-parity (spec/70 item-08) : all @shared structs byte-identical SPIR-V · DXIL · MSL · WGSL
                    on 20-module test corpus (max diff = 0)
    ASSERT.P4.07 · owned-DXIL-emitter (stage-2 per spec/14) compiles 100% of canonical pipeline against AMPAS reference
                    (no dxc subproc dep · validator-identical to dxc output for matching-features subset)
    ASSERT.P4.08 · owned-SPIR-V-emitter (stage-1+ per spec/14) emits validator-identical to spirv-val ALL targets
                    (zero rspirv runtime dep)
  ⟧

