§I MEMORY-DOMAIN · spec/65-GPU-memory-types in-use
  ⟦
    (full spec : 65_GPU_MEMORY_TYPE_DISTINCTION.csl)

    Used-throughout-this-plan per spec/65 type-system :
      gpu<T>       · GPU-resident · cannot CPU-deref · used for : Buffer<f32> · Texture · DescriptorSet
      shared<T>    · ReBAR-mapped · CPU+GPU both access · used for : per-frame uniforms (FrameUniforms)
                                                                       light-list ring-buffer · readback debug-probe
      staged<T>    · CPU-side staging · used for : asset-upload (PNG/GLTF texture → gpu<Texture>)
      transfer<T>  · in-flight transfer · used for : async-upload pipeline (staged → commit → gpu)
      semaphore    · queue-sync · timeline-semaphore used for cross-queue (graphics ↔ compute)

    Per-pass mapping :
      depth-prepass        : reads gpu<MeshIndex> + gpu<TransformPool> ; writes gpu<DepthTexture>
      light-cull (compute) : reads gpu<DepthTexture> Hi-Z + shared<LightList, WeakOrdered> ;
                              writes gpu<TileLightIndices>
      opaque-main          : reads gpu<DepthTexture> + gpu<TileLightIndices> + gpu<MaterialAtlas> ;
                              writes gpu<HdrColorTexture>
      transparent          : reads gpu<HdrColorTexture> + gpu<DepthTexture> ;
                              writes gpu<HdrColorTexture> (alpha-blend)
      post-tonemap         : reads gpu<HdrColorTexture> ; writes gpu<SwapchainBackbuffer>

    ReBAR detection :
      cssl-host-d3d12 + cssl-host-vulkan probe at init ; alloc_shared falls back to staged<T> per spec/65 FM.01
      per stdlib/gpu.cssl loa_frame_latency=1 + IDXGISwapChain2::SetMaximumFrameLatency(1) waitable-swap-chain

    PRIME-DIRECTIVE check :
      Sensitive<gaze|face|body|biometric> absolute-banned across PCIe per spec/65 GPU0007 (P3.W3 gaze-collapse compliance)
      Cap<Shared> + Cap<TransferAuth> required for shared<T> + cross-domain transfers (P2.W2 async-compute)
  ⟧

§I PROPRIETARY-DIFFERENTIATION · what-this-stack-claims-over-Unity/Unreal/Bevy/Godot
  ⟦
    (per spec/56 § DIFFERENTIATION + spec/59 § STRATEGIC-FRAMING)

    1. EFFECTS-FIRST-CLASS  (per spec/04)
       · {GpuInit · GpuSubmit · Deadline<N> · Realtime<Crit>} threaded structurally in fn-sigs
       · compiler proves frame-budget via SMT-discharge (spec/20)
       · no AAA-engine has this · Bevy doesn't · Unity GC-pauses ; Unreal C++ no static effect-tracking

    2. REFINEMENT-TYPES  (per spec/03 · per item-14)
       · {v : f32 | 0.0 ≤ v ≤ 1.0} for shader-bound params · static-checked
       · radians vs degrees confusion at type-level
       · no AAA-engine has this

    3. BUILT-IN AUTODIFF  (per spec/05 + spec/17 Jet<T,N>)
       · differentiable shading + neural-radiance + physics-sim AS-FIRST-CLASS
       · enables P3.W3 gaze-velocity-prediction via Jet AD-tape directly in MIR
       · no AAA-engine has this in-language ; PyTorch3D/Mitsuba require external Python

    4. MULTI-GPU-FROM-ONE-SOURCE  (per spec/02 + spec/14)
       · single MIR · 4 GPU codegen paths (SPIR-V · DXIL · MSL · WGSL)
       · cross-target-struct-parity (item-08) makes @shared structs byte-identical 4 ways
       · Unity/Unreal have multi-backend but per-shader-language ; CSSL has per-IR-emitter

    5. CSL-SYMBIOSIS  (per CLAUDE.md global + spec/16)
       · CSL3 is the human/AI thinking-notation that becomes CSSL the program-notation
       · density-advantage for AI-collaboration (per spec/58 measured 900-1200 LOC/hr velocity)
       · proprietary moat : AI-fleet-velocity vs traditional team-velocity

    6. SOVEREIGNTY-BY-CONSTRUCTION  (per PRIME_DIRECTIVE + spec/11 + spec/12 + spec/65)
       · Cap<Gpu> witness default-deny at compile + runtime
       · Sensitive<X> IFC labels propagate structurally · compile-refuse at biometric-egress
       · no DRM · no rootkit · no telemetry-by-default
       · zero rented runtimes (LLVM-out · Rust-out at runtime per Phase-E)
       · spec/65 GPU0007 absolute-ban biometric across PCIe · NO Cap-override possible

    7. SUBSTRATE-EFFECT-PASS DIFFERENTIATION  (per spec/32 V.1..V.6 opt-in)
       · spectral-render (16-band hyperspectral · NEVER RGB until tonemap)
       · gaze-reactive observation-collapse (Heisenberg-style · ψ-collapse around fixation-point)
       · mise-en-abyme (true-recursive-ray-cast · scene-within-mirror is-ACTUALLY-the-scene)
       · sub-pixel fractal-tessellation (KAN-weight displacement · looks-natural-not-noisy)
       · NO shipped game uses these · unique LoA marker

    These differentiations are LOAD-BEARING for the spec/56 § DIFFERENTIATION strategic moat.
    They DO NOT come for free · this plan budgets each ASSERT against frame-budget honestly.
  ⟧

